From 6f7e9e2854388bd76459ea56bbefbeab6ca0f560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhayali <273542685+Abdelhayali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:34:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] CUDA MMVQ: Tesla V100 (sm_70) tuning for i-quant decode /
 speculative verify

- Volta parameter table (MMVQ_PARAMETERS_VOLTA): Turing values plus per-type overrides in mmvq-v100.cuh.
- IQ3_S/IQ3_XXS/IQ2_S/IQ2_XS/IQ2_XXS: codebook staged in shared memory (global lookups were the bottleneck,
  ~30-40% of DRAM bandwidth), also for the fused gate projection; 4 rows per block (Q3_K too).
- IQ3_S/IQ3_XXS 2-8 token verify: decode each weight block once, reuse for every token column (bit-identical).
- Only for dense matrices (template flag v100_dense); MoE expert matrices keep the stock kernel.
- test-backend-ops perf cases at Qwen3.8-27B ffn shapes.

Measured on one V100-SXM2-16GB, Qwen3.8-27B UD-IQ3_S: tg 30.6 -> 33.1 t/s (+8%), pp4 +7.5%, pp8 +6.5%;
IQ3_S GEMV 107 -> 81 us. test-backend-ops MUL_MAT + MUL_MAT_ID: 3376/3376 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
