Subject: [PATCH 2/2] CUDA V100: split fused gate+up for smem-codebook
 i-quants, IQ4_XS 4 rows per block

On Volta the fused gate+up MMVQ kernel needs twice the registers and is slower than two tuned launches for
IQ3_S/IQ3_XXS/IQ2_* (IQ3_S 184 us fused vs 2 x 81 us). IQ4_XS: 4 rows per block, 3-8% faster per GEMV.
Qwen3.8-27B UD-IQ3_S on one V100: tg 30.6 (stock) -> 33.7 t/s. test-backend-ops: 16562 tests OK, 0 FAIL
(one FLASH_ATTN_EXT mma config has no sm_70 code, pre-existing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
